d then I was  able to gradually get it down actually  the same day I did it for a while and I  got it down to four minutes and 41  seconds  so if you're just starting out and  you're solving it in 20 minutes give  yourself a little bit of time solve it  more and you'll eventually get it down  that first day probably within half the  time that you got it the first time you  solve it so overall this cube has been  pretty good the stickers I think held up  better than they did on this cube  because I didn't spray this one with the  petroleum distillates so after I was  able to solve this cube within around I  think three minutes I then went on to  the 5x5 rubik's cube professor and this  is the first professor that i ever  purchased as you can tell it's pretty  beat up as well some of the stickers on  some of the sides don't peel and then  some of the ones on the other sides do  so I have three sides that are peeling  and three sides that are pretty decent  which is kind of weird but anyway I had  to crazy glue these stickers back on and  I broke this piece here but this was not  one of my favorite 5x5 keeps to solve it  was actually really good at turning but  instead of buying a new piece from cube  Smith which I didn't know about back  then I just went on to buy a new cube  since I broke that piece so this is  basically the same exact model for of  the Rubik's professor it's not the exact  same one that they have out now which  they retooled and I'll show you what I  got from the rubik's company in a little  bit so after I was able to solve the 5x5  I believe the first time that I ever  solved that I got around 12 minutes and  then I was able to gradually get it down  within like a week or so I got it down  to around nine minutes and then within  two months I got it down to six and  around five and a half in about two and  a half months so give yourself some time  keep practicing and you'll eventually  drop the time down after I was able to  solve the 5x5 the 4x4 the 3x3 I had the  whole rubik's family I decided to give  the East Sheen cube to try so these are  basically cubes that are made in China  and they're pretty decent cubes actually  for speed selling they turn pretty well  and they're actually a lot cheaper than  the Rubik's brand now this cube is  really a lot smaller than this 5x5 as  you'll see this cube is actually close  to being the same size as the 3x3 so the  five by five East chin cube and the four  by four East chin cube are exactly the  same size and I got these both from  China and it took around three to four  weeks to get it I remember waiting for  it for a while so don't order from China  I actually this cube here is broken I  dropped it and the axis center piece it  cracked off and I actually crazy glued  it back on so it still print spins  pretty nicely but you can see that this  is this is actually broken here so I  don't really use this cube too much  anymore I decided to go on and buy  another set of another East Chien 5x5  cube and this time I bought it from  puzzle pros and this cube is is really  good I still use this cube a lot which  is why it's a more worn down than the  older one and I also bought a 3x3  do-it-yourself cube so when you get the  east gene cubes you'll actually get them  in these little boxes depending on which  model you get you could probably get it  with the plastic as well and it does  come with instructions on how to put it  back together because they are  do-it-yourself cubes so the  do-it-yourself 3x3 that I bought from  puzzle pros was a really good buy this  cube is is really good its quick it  spins nicely and once you lubricate it  with a little bit of silicone spray it  spins really nicely let me show you guys  so it's a really good cube and I'm glad  I bought it so after I bought that then  you know that I bought the the V cubes  the 6 and the 7 so if you haven't  already checked out the V Cube reviews  that I gave I gave an in-depth review of  the ups and downs o